- 0.2.2 (2026-07-11): three fixes baked in after deploying elearning-platform
  (built from this template) to Dokploy hit them for real: (1) web's
  docker-compose.yml build args now resolve NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL from the
  host env (was hardcoded to the dev default, so it silently couldn't be
  overridden without editing the compose file) — Next inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_*
  at `next build` time, so a runtime env is always too late and ships an
  empty API URL, causing mixed-content failures on an HTTPS deploy;
  apps/web/Dockerfile's existing ARG/ENV now carries an explanatory comment
  of the same gotcha. (2) apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx documents (commented,
  since the family is project-specific) loading web fonts via a runtime
  `<head><link>` instead of `next/font/google` — the web Docker build stage
  has no network egress to fonts.googleapis.com, so `next/font/google`
  throws at `next build` and fails the image build. (3) new
  docker-compose.dokploy.yml: a self-contained Dokploy compose overlay
  (Dokploy's label injector doesn't expand compose `include:`) mirroring
  db/api/web/redis/worker (minio/minio-mc dropped — dev-only S3 emulator,
  prod points at real R2/S3) with `dokploy-network` (external) added and
  `api` on both `default` and `dokploy-network` — Dokploy's per-domain
  network injection otherwise replaces a domain'd service's `networks:`
  entirely, silently cutting `api` off from `db`/`redis` and breaking
  Prisma with connection error P1001 the moment `api` gets a domain.
